# ACloudViewer Plugin Development Rules

## Plugin Architecture

- Plugins live under `plugins/core/Standard/` (standard) or `plugins/core/IO/` (I/O filters)
- Each plugin needs: `CMakeLists.txt`, `info.json`, a `.qrc` resource file
- Use `AddPlugin(NAME ...)` from `plugins/cmake/Plugins.cmake`
- Plugins link: `CVCoreLib`, `CVPluginAPI`, `CVPluginStub`

## AICore-Based Plugins (mandatory)

Read `.agents/skills/acloudviewer-aicore-plugin/SKILL.md` for the complete
integration workflow and acceptance gates, especially its `references/`
documents for reuse ownership and executable accuracy/performance profiles.

- First decide whether the plugin consumes an existing task, extends a model
  family, or requires a genuinely new input/output/lifecycle contract. A new UI
  or product name alone does not justify a new AICore task.
- The plugin is a thin Qt/application adapter: input/source selection, worker
  invocation, annotations/DB entities, rendering, and export. Model graphs,
  preprocessing, backend policy, cache ownership, and numeric postprocessing
  stay in AICore.
- Link `AICore` and include only public `aicore/*` headers. Never include ggml or
  task-private headers from a plugin.
- Register the plugin option/target in the central plugin CMake entry, ship
  `info.json`/resources/README, and add incremental `BUILD.md` and plugin-index
  rows. When automation is in scope, extend the existing JSON-RPC and
  `cli-anything-acloudviewer` mapping/tests rather than adding private CLI flags.
- Reuse `ecvAICoreRuntimeHelpers.h`, `ecvAICoreUiHelper.h`, shared video
  components, `ecvTestDataRepository`, and the AICore-exported model catalog.
  Never add plugin-private device locks, model URL/digest tables, downloader
  implementations, cache roots, or decoded-image preprocessing pipelines.
  Plugins may feed exported catalog metadata to the shared
  `ecvModelDownloader` / `ecvAssetIntegrity` services.
- Worker results carry source identity and generation. Contexts stay on the
  worker thread; pending teardown follows the shared helper. Live pipelines
  keep one running frame plus at most one latest pending frame and call
  `completeFrameProcessing()` on every completion path.
- Use borrowed `aicore_image_view` with the real `bytesPerLine()` and format;
  use typed results with their documented release function. File, encoded-image,
  and JSON round-trips are compatibility/export paths, not frame inference.
- Plugin helper tests do not replace the headless task gate. Verify the actual
  still/live/cancel/stale/error/teardown workflow after AICore truth, parity,
  repeated-forward, and validation-manifest coverage pass.
- Run `python3 core/AICore/tests/check_plugin_aicore_boundaries.py --root .
  --strict`; it must pass repository-wide, not only for new plugins.

## Key Interfaces

- `ccStdPluginInterface` — base class for standard plugins
- `ecvMainAppInterface` — access to app (DB, views, console, selection)
- `ccCommandLineInterface` — register CLI commands via `registerCommand()`
- `ecvDisplayTools` — static display operations (redraw, view matrix, etc.)

## Common Patterns

- Get app interface: `m_app` (set via `setMainAppInterface()`)
- Access DB root: `m_app->dbRootObject()`
- Cast entities: `ccHObjectCaster::ToPointCloud(obj)`, `ccHObjectCaster::ToMesh(obj)`
- Force redraw: `ecvDisplayTools::RedrawDisplay()`
- View orientations: `CC_TOP_VIEW`, `CC_FRONT_VIEW`, `CC_ISO_VIEW_1`, etc.

## Build

```bash
cmake -DPLUGIN_STANDARD_QJSONRPC=ON -DPLUGIN_STANDARD_QSIBR=ON ..
make -j$(nproc)
```

## Entity Types

| Enum | Type |
|------|------|
| `CV_TYPES::POINT_CLOUD` | Point cloud |
| `CV_TYPES::MESH` | Triangle mesh |
| `CV_TYPES::POLY_LINE` | Polyline |
| `CV_TYPES::HIERARCHY_OBJECT` | Group/container |
